# Local-only.  The rule for everything below is the same: it is either not
# ours to publish, or it is a cache that can be rebuilt, or it is machine state
# that would only ever cause a conflict.

# --- 6.0 GB of whisper model cache.  Rebuildable, and no repo wants it. ---
_tools/models/

# --- ripped game assets: 214 MB + a 212 MB zip.  Not ours to publish, and the
#     zip is over GitHub's 100 MB hard file limit anyway. ---
TRG Sounds & Images pack/
TRG Sounds & Images pack.zip

# --- 104 MB of third-party YouTube guides, downloaded only so they could be
#     transcribed locally.  Copyrighted, and they are not part of the project. ---
Videos/

# --- paste / inbox / vision caches from the local vision bridge ---
.ai/

# --- the Studio <-> disk byte channel's scratch space.  _pull/ holds copies
#     PULLED OUT of Studio to be compared against src/; they are duplicates by
#     construction, so committing them would create a second copy of every
#     module that can drift from the one that actually runs.  The comparison is
#     the product, not the copies. ---
_tools/_pull/

# --- server logs from _tools/receive.py and _tools/serve.py.  Machine state on
#     a localhost port: it records when THIS session pulled what, which is not a
#     fact about the project and would conflict on every machine. ---
_tools/_attic/logs/

# --- machine-local claude state (the shared settings.json, if one is ever
#     added, is deliberately NOT ignored) ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# --- OS and editor cruft ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# --- the room watcher's per-run instance dump (Data/roomwatch*/inventory.txt).
#     Every run's copy is BYTE-IDENTICAL to every other run's -- all seven so
#     far, md5 5ae9ab97526f39b3fbe530d12f97f6f3, 5278228 bytes -- because it is
#     a snapshot of a world nobody edited between runs.  It is 5.3 MB a copy and
#     seven copies is 37 MB of the same file.  Nothing downstream reads it:
#     rooms.txt (5.7 KB) is the derived answer and it IS tracked, and the dump
#     can be regenerated by running the watcher again. ---
Data/roomwatch*/inventory.txt
